VERDICT: ASTRA RIGHT

Judged committed HEAD `96a44fe3` only. The helper's S-format biconditional is false. Astra's underflow term is the exact change-set. The helper's D-subnormal sentence is right and does not repair the S term.

`new` is `ieee_store_float_value` (`regress/diff_ieee_store.c:193`, `:386`, `:415`), which calls `ieee_store_float_value_rm(..., IEEE_RM_LEGACY)` (`src/core/float_emul.c:713-715`). `old` is `store_old` (`regress/diff_ieee_store.c:100`). All four inputs are above `2^-1022`, so both sides take `FP_NORMAL` (`diff_ieee_store.c:123`, `float_emul.c:517`).

Sign is stored first (`diff_ieee_store.c:113-114`, `float_emul.c:499-501`), then the magnitude is taken (`diff_ieee_store.c:124-125`, `float_emul.c:518-519`). `orig` keeps the signed input (`float_emul.c:427-428`). S bias is 127 (`diff_ieee_store.c:134`, `float_emul.c:590`). `2^-150` biases to `-23` and clamps to 0. `2^-140` biases to `-13` and clamps to 0 (`diff_ieee_store.c:135-136`, `float_emul.c:591-592`). Old then assigns `r = 0` (`diff_ieee_store.c:145-146`) and clears the sign. New keeps the sign and ORs `ieee_encode_subnormal(orig, S, LEGACY)` (`float_emul.c:663-665`). LEGACY truncates `ldexp(orig, 149)` (`float_emul.c:377`, `:380-381`) and then takes the magnitude (`float_emul.c:385-386`).

| input | scaled | trunc magnitude | old | new | helper | Astra |
|---|---|---|---|---|---|---|
| `-2^-150` | `-0.5` | `0` | `0x00000000` | `0x80000000` | false | true |
| `+2^-150` | `+0.5` | `0` | `0x00000000` | `0x00000000` | false | false |
| `-2^-140` | `-512` | `0x200` | `0x00000000` | `0x80000200` | true | true |
| `+2^-140` | `+512` | `0x200` | `0x00000000` | `0x00000200` | true | true |

`trunc(-0.5)` is `-0.0`. `-0.0 < 0.0` is false, so the magnitude stays 0 and the cast ORs nothing. The sign kept at `float_emul.c:664` remains `0x80000000`. `2^-140` sits in `(2^-149, 2^-126)`. Both predicates accept it, and both signs differ.

`trunc(|x| * 2^149)` is 0 exactly when `|x| < 2^-149`, and at least 1 when `|x| >= 2^-149` (`2^-149` scales to 1). Positive sub-quantum inputs agree. Negative sub-quantum inputs differ. At and above that quantum, both signs differ from old's cleared word. `|x| == 2^-126` has biased exponent 1, skips `float_emul.c:663`, and both sides emit `0x00800000` / `0x80800000`. Host subnormals stay out through `isnormal`: old returns the sign alone (`diff_ieee_store.c:148-149`), and new's subnormal arm (`float_emul.c:668-677`) scales a magnitude below `2^-1022` by `2^149` into a value below `2^-873`, which truncates to 0 and leaves the same signed zero. The `0 < abs(x)` conjunct adds no inputs once `isnormal` is present.

The helper text copies `must_differ` (`diff_ieee_store.c:303-304`). The comment at `:296-301` says a sub-quantum input agrees with upstream. That is true for positive inputs only. The sweep still counts every `0 < |x| < 2^-126` difference as underflow (`diff_ieee_store.c:420`), so `-2^-150` is neither unexplained nor missed.

On D, old's subnormal arm stores only the sign (`diff_ieee_store.c:148-149`, sign at bit 63 via `:109`). New ORs `ieee_encode_subnormal` (`float_emul.c:668-677`), and `ldexp` by 1074 (`float_emul.c:377`) restores the integer significand `1 .. 2^52-1`. Every D subnormal differs. `dD > 0` is the committed check (`diff_ieee_store.c:1302-1303`, `:1289-1294`).
